# (`require_code_owner_review`) is off in the `main` ruleset, now "main: pull request, Copilot,
# CodeQL", and in its copy for develop, "develop: pull request, Copilot, CodeQL" (T-15b). Since 2026-10-10 the owner has turned Copilot review off for
# develop; the ruleset names are kept. Leave
# it off in both: the only code owner is also the author of every pull request, and GitHub does
# not count an author's approval of their own pull request (GitHub's documented rule; not tested
# here), so with no bypass actor in either ruleset (none today) turning it on would block every
# merge.
